# UI & UX Rules — Aquarius DeFi Lab

## Design Philosophy
- Clarity over cleverness.
- Reduce cognitive load at every step.
- The user should always know what to do next.

## Components
- Use Shadcn/UI where applicable.
- All components must be accessible by default.
- Prefer composition over deeply nested components.

## Language
- Avoid protocol jargon unless necessary.
- Prefer human-readable explanations over raw metrics.

## State & Feedback
- Every action must produce visible feedback.
- Loading, error, and empty states are mandatory.

## Visual Hierarchy
- Highlight outcomes, not features.
- Make the primary action obvious.


## Summary (Non-Negotiable)
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- Prefer Shadcn/UI components when applicable.
- All UI components must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard).
- UI must never contain business logic.
- Dashboards visualize signals — they do not compute them.
- Frontend should degrade gracefully if streams are unavailable.
